they are the almost forgotten victims of  the early days of the war in ukraine  yeven vusic has kept watch as they stand  in an anonymous freezer van in an  anonymous car park in this unit alone 12  bodies still not identified still not  claimed by their loved ones  we would like to bury these people it is  a long time they have been lying here  more than three months relatives are  coming here and they are shocked they  cannot identify the body simply by  looking of them  many people left for other countries so  these victims are lying here unclaimed  in other units nearby 30 soldiers and  another one 40 other civilians some  recovered from deep in a nearby forest  the russians built their positions in  this wood facing towards kiev when they  were forced to withdraw that's when  investigators moved in and they found  one mass grave and they think around  here there will be many more  just last month ukrainian forensic teams  found the site and started gathering  evidence they pulled seven bodies from a  tiny grave each victim shot in the head  and dumped their crime being male and  old enough to fight against the russians  evan vusick was there that day helping  out watching the ground give up its  secrets  at the moment i sleep okay but when i  excuse the bodies of children even  though they are not my children and i do  have two children it's horrible because  even with alcohol i can get it out of my  mind  from each victim they've taken dna one  day their family might claim them give  them a proper burial  the man heading the police investigation  into what happened  told me no matter how difficult these  crimes must be investigated  this should be important not just  ukrainians but to the whole  international community this is very  important the same as the investigations  into what happened during world war ii  we must investigate the army of the  russian federation the army commanders  this message should be delivered  the bodies will sit for a few more weeks  then they will be quietly buried but for  now they set silent witnesses in an  investigation into war crimes and murder  alan fisher al-jazeera marotzka ukraine
 

